  "conclusion": "No attributable steady-state throughput gain. Both paths complete every case with rows == distinct == sent. Engine is ~+4% at 80k offered (absence of the 100ms flush-boundary tail), -0.2%/-0.3% at 400k/1M (queue/refcount overhead, within noise). The old synchronous flush already exceeds 30k by >25x on this synthetic TTAP workload; a company 3-5k/s symptom must be diagnosed in its schema/synchronous mode/record processing, not assumed to be flush serialization. Engine value is decoupling, backpressure and observability.",
